#: 01_mace_intro.md:1
msgid "Machine-learned potentials for atomistic simulations"
msgstr "Atomistic Simulations のための Machine-learned Potentials"

#: 01_mace_intro.md:3
msgid ""
"Over the past two decades, a drastic change has emerged in the way we "
"simulate atomistic systems. Machine-learned potentials (MLPs) have enabled "
"*ab-initio*-level accuracy in force and energy predictions for a fraction of"
" the cost associated with traditional methods. We can now access systems of "
"a size and complexity that were previously inaccessible to first-princples "
"simulation. An overview of some of the major MLP developments and "
"achievements can be found in this recent introductory review: [Introduction "
"to machine learning potentials for atomistic "
"simulations](https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.00626)"
msgstr ""
"過去20年の間に、Atomistic Systems のシミュレーション手法は大きく変わった。Machine-learned "
"Potentials（MLPs）により、従来法の計算コストのごく一部で、Force と Energy を *ab-initio* "
"水準の精度で予測できるようになった。これまで First-principles Simulation "
"では扱えなかった規模や複雑さの系にも到達できる。MLP の主な発展と成果の概要は、最近の入門 Review [Introduction to "
"machine learning potentials for atomistic "
"simulations](https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.00626) にまとめられている。"

#: 01_mace_intro.md:5
msgid ""
"At the forefront of MLP development is the Multi Atomic Cluster Expansion "
"(MACE) framework [1](https://arxiv.org/abs/2206.07697). Developed in 2022, "
"this model combines a complete high body order polynomial basis, the so-"
"called Atomic Cluster Expansion, with a message-passing tensoral network. "
"This architecture provides learnable representations of semi-local chemical "
"environments to accurately reproduce reference *ab initio* energies and "
"forces."
msgstr ""
"MLP 開発の最前線にあるのが Multi Atomic Cluster Expansion（MACE）フレームワーク "
"[1](https://arxiv.org/abs/2206.07697) である。2022年に開発されたこのモデルは、Atomic Cluster "
"Expansion と呼ばれる、完全な High-body-order Polynomial Basis を Message-passing "
"Tensor Network と組み合わせている。この Architecture は Semi-local Chemical Environments "
"の学習可能な表現を与え、参照する *ab initio* の Energies と Forces を精密に再現する。"

#: 01_mace_intro.md:7
msgid ""
"For this tutorial we will make use of a pre-trained MACE model, provided "
"within this repository. This model can describe gaseous carbonic acid and "
"has been trained on GGA-level DFT reference data. For more details on how to"
" train MACE models for your own system of interest, we refer to [MACE "
"tutorials](https://mace-"
"docs.readthedocs.io/en/latest/examples/tutorials.html)."
msgstr ""
"このチュートリアルでは、リポジトリに付属する学習済みの MACE モデルを使う。このモデルは気相の炭酸を記述でき、GGA 水準の DFT "
"参照データで学習している。自身の対象系に対して MACE モデルを学習する方法の詳細は、[MACE tutorials](https://mace-"
"docs.readthedocs.io/en/latest/examples/tutorials.html) を参照してほしい。"
